## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | flutter_app/lib/network/network_session.dart | 🚨 blocking replyto queue receipt collapse only covers realtime arrivals — history loading still renders the triple queued cards this pr promises to remove the new collapse rule lives exclusively inside channelstate add flutter app lib network network session dart 110 143 it is applied from both realtime paths — onenvelope network session dart 727 and ondmmail network session dm dart → state add which is why the new tests and goldens pass but the history path bypasses add entirely loadhistorypage network session dart 405 410 does its own seen add envelope id state messages insertall 0 decoded — no receipt collapse no legacy replyto inference refreshafterreconnect network session dart 757 766 clears messages and seen and rebuilds every open channel from the rest tail page through that same bypass consequences 1 the dominant repro of the exact bug this pr claims to fix pr info md убраны тройные queued карточки is the offline scenario the agent mailbox is asleep the user retries n times while away → the hub persists n queued receipts with n distinct envelope ids and the same replyto → the user reopens the app → the chat page loads history → n queue cards render again only current version peers put replyto in the persisted plaintext legacy 1 0 751 history rows aren t even normalized 2 the realtime collapse is not durable the next reconnect refreshafterreconnect wipes the store and re expands every collapsed card from hub history — even without an app restart evidence that this is reachable in practice decodedmenvelope does populate replyto for history rows the dmdecoded plumbing lands in decode → loadhistorypage so the data needed to collapse is present — only the rule is not applied there nothing at the ui layer compensates channel chat service dart projects channelstate messages 1 1 with no collapse suggested fix small same file extract the queued receipt collapse the duplicate check replyto normalization network session dart 110 143 into a channelstate helper and apply it when building the decoded page list in loadhistorypage — collapsing within the page block and against rows already in the store — so realtime and history agree please also cover it with a test that feeds the second page through loadhistorypage instead of state add directly the current tests all build state via add which is exactly the path that works |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

